["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isbn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Book Number (ISBN)](https://www.isbn-international.org/content/isbn-users-manual/29) is a unique numeric identifier for monographic publications standardized by [ISO 2108](https://www.iso.org/standard/65483.html). It consists of either 10 digits (for assignments prior to January 1, 2007) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISBN is composed of five parts: a GS1 prefix, a registration group, a registrant, a publication element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9780198836063`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifier", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A reference to a resource identifier defined outside the scope of SPDX 3 content that uniquely identifies an Element.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Dataset/datasetAvailability", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Dataset/DatasetAvailabilityType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/Artifact", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property", "_:N5adfdeea88c346968550f2456834eeda", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isni", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Name Identifier (ISNI)](https://isni.org/page/what-is-isni/) is a unique identifier used to distinguish the public identities of parties involved in the creation, production, and distribution of media content. Standardized by [ISO 27729](https://www.iso.org/standard/87177.html), it consists of 16 characters\u201415 digits plus a final check character\u2014and is often represented as a URI, such as `https://isni.org/isni/000000012146438X`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N9da09cd5dba140b8bdcecf8ec72fcbbc", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/extension", "globalId", "", ""]
